A||||44||Lady Pegasus||FIERORAMA PICS!!!||||5||
Z||000000||Lady Pegasus||09-09-2001||10:05 PM||||Well, let's see.  Fierorama ended, FOUR HOURS AGO!!  And yet, nothing!!  I know not EVERYBODY had a long drive home.  What, no one wants to talk about the LOVELY weather we had?  HA!!  Anyhow, got to meet MinngreenGT, Moo Cow, monkeyman, and many others.  It was a great show.  116 BEAUTIFUL (and NOT so beautiful) Fiero's.  All in all, I had a great time.  Feel free to discuss, just thought I'd get the ball rolling.<P>------------------<BR>Hey pretty....don't you wanna take a ride with me...through my world?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Lady Pegasus||09-09-2001||10:07 PM||||And PLEASE!!  Don't mention ANYTHING about Haze and his INDY on tv...we don't want his head to explode. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Hey pretty....don't you wanna take a ride with me...through my world?||||reg||4
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-09-2001||10:34 PM||||I just got home.  I could have lived without the rain, but I had a great time.  Just remember...I-1.  It was great meeting so many PFF members.  I'd name all that I met, but I'm sure I'd accidentally omit someone.  I had a chance to have dinner with Oreif, Gargoyle, Haze Performance, Leadfoot, Jack (of all trades) (sorry, Scott.  I forgot your username!) and their families.  Haze is now a movie star.  ("What kind of car do you have?  Uh.  Umm.  Hmm."  Did the spandex lady with the feather distract you, Haze??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )  <P>Haze won some awards for a couple of his cars including his awesome Indy.  Oreif also won in his class (Modified--killer car for those of you who haven't seen it).  I missed out on winning the Ttop car but won a $500 gift certificate to The Fiero Store.  I still can't believe I won anything.  I can't wait until I get off of work tomorrow.  I'm going shopping!!<P>I'll post some pics tomorrow after work.  I'm way too tired to download them tonight.<P>Thanx to all who made Fierorama a great time.  And a big thanx to Oreif who not only provided dinner and drinks on Saturday night, but also guided me to his house and to the show.  (I hate it when I get misdirected.)<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000003||jch82||09-09-2001||11:08 PM||||This should get things started. I had a blast! There was a little bit of rain but that didn't stop anything. It was great! I even got to bring my fiero to her first show....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000022(1).jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000040(1).jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000043(1)_1.jpg"> <P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82(sig).jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Oreif||09-09-2001||11:18 PM||||Aside from the rain it was EXCELLENT!!<BR>Congrats to all the winners who are on here.<BR>Monkeyman: Class Winner, High Mileage 1986, and of course the $500 Fiero Store Certificate!<BR>Gargoyle: Class Winner<BR>LeadFoot: Class Winner<BR>Me: Class Winner<BR>MinnGreenGT: Class Winner (I'm Making your emblems.)<BR>OOPS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  Sorry 87Pegasus!<BR>87Pegasus: Class Winner.<BR>Haze: 2 Class Winner (Indy in one class and 85 coupe in another class)<P>Saturday was great (Stayed up way too late!)<BR>Here is Haze being interviewed!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(I'll Email you all the full size pics in the morning)<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze01.jpg">   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze02.jpg">   <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">      <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B><P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||87 Pegasus||09-10-2001||12:35 AM||||Hey Oreif you forgot about me....  :-(  i was a class winner...  what the Little people don't get to play with the big boys... you just wait til i get my Pegasus back on...then we will see...  haha   so be on the look out...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> I'll Be Back...  :-)  Just wait a few years and when you see the mini batmobile come up be hind you we will see who runs... (I just bought the blue prints tonight i should be getting them in a few weeks)<P>------------------<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!||||reg||9
Z||000006||Smoooooth GT||09-10-2001||12:44 AM||||Great to see the people behind the car's...<BR>I wish I could have been there.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierodave||09-10-2001||12:58 AM||||I have seen that Indy Before!    Congrats to all that won!<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tina||09-10-2001||03:28 AM||||Wow,...we made it home...sleep......rtthyrdtyjuttudxhrticjhutijyyijygrd  sorry   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"> <BR>Little nap <BR>Anyways ,had a great time and congrats to all  who made it.<P>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||09-10-2001||04:43 AM||||I would like to thank all the little people that made this possible. I will be selling 8x10 autographed photos on my website. Now that I'm a TV celebrity, I can give that Mrs. Illinois a run for her money.. lol j/k<P><B>-Congrats-</B><P>Oreif- You go get-em (You know who I'm talking about)<P>Monkeyman- You the man!!!! (It was great meeting you & your wife)<P>LeadFoot- It was nice to meet you @ Daves.<P>MinnGreenGT- Very Nice Car. <P>Gargoyle- (My fellow screen door destroyer. lol)<FONT SIZE="1">Inside Joke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> </FONT><P>87 Pegasus- Good job getting the car ready for the show.<P>-------------------------------------<BR><B>-Special thanks to-</B><P>Blake Bandusky (You know what you did Big Guy.. <P>Fiero_24- Thanks for driving one of the cars home for me. <P>Orief- For the pics & the display item you gave me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>KissMySSFiero- For the gift you brought me. You better buy your little brother a hell of a gift for holding it the entire way down. Tell him that I forgive him for not pulling my ticket for the raffle car. lol   <P>mope- For bringing the decal to the show. (Sorry I missed you after thr show. Let me know if you get the money today. If not, Ill send out another one)  <P>Fiero-John- For the Indy Press Pass.<P>And last but not least. The lovley Lady Pegasus for finding it in her heart to make fun of me all day.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>-------------------------------------<P>Tina- Nice meeting you. Your car is awsome!!<P>-------------------------------------<BR> <BR>During the award ceremonies N.I.F.E. gives out awards to a representative of all the Fiero Clubs that attended. We had quite a few people there from Pennocks. I'm going to try to get Pennocks recognized next year. Whoever accepts the award can send it to Cliff.  <BR> <P><I>-Haze</I>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">             <BR></A><BR><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||6
Z||000010||KissMySSFiero||09-10-2001||07:39 AM||||Haze.<BR>no problem for the hitch, thanks for the light. ill tell justin you forgive him.  <BR>i still dont forgive him for not picking me.  little bastard.  j/k   it was a lot of fun.  i didnt win anything.  i cant win.  i figured i would at least get highest milage with 171,000 on an 88 or most wrecked.  but some chick got that because her car was wrecked 15years ago and fixed.  (that pissed me off)  because i saw her car.  she got an award for the SE class because her car looked so good.  oh well i had fun anyways even with the rain.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fiero_24||09-10-2001||08:10 AM||||Haze, no need to thank me.  After really being pissed about not having my 87GT there it was nice to drive away in a Fiero even if it was not the raffle car.  Nice meeting everyone also.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR>  [<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||6
Z||000012||Oreif||09-10-2001||08:13 AM||||87 Pegasus: I'm very sorry I forgot you!!<BR>(Edited above to show correctly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">   )<P><BR>||||reg||11
Z||000013||Leadfoot||09-10-2001||09:34 AM||||I must say that for my first experience in a fiero show....I had a great time.  I felt right at home.  Saturday at Oreif's started the whole weekend off.  I meet Haze, Monkeyman, Gargoyle...and I believe Scott (sorry but I am bad with names).  Finally a group of "nice" people that say good things about fieros.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Talk about a fire hazard though...there was a total of 6 fieros on Oreifs property.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  As for the show I had a great time looking at the cars and talking to their owners.  However, most of my time was spent near Tina's car.  It sure is one heck of a nice fiero....sounds as good as it looks too.  Thumbs up to her and her husband.  Also, I meet another of Oreifs friends...great bunch of guys.  Oreif, it must be nice having fellow co-workers that drive fieros.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Congratulation to the all class winners.  I for one sure did not expect to win anything (o.k. maybe a chicken McNugget from Mickey D's).  I'd like to thank everyone that voted.  Must have been that big glossy I had of Ms. Illinois sitting on my hood.  <IMG SRC="http://www.contrabandent.com/pez1/otn/laughing/yelrotflmao.gif">   Boy I can hardly wait for the next show! The fiero community just plain rocks! ||||reg||1
Z||000014||lowfierogt||09-10-2001||09:40 AM||||Sounds like a great show.   I got stuck being on-call for work.   It would have been fun to go.   <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/87%20fiero_files/Jun0302.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000015||MinnGreenGT||09-10-2001||09:55 AM||||Well, after traveling between 80-90mph the entire way (plus a stop for dinner and gas), we arrived back home at 11:35pm.  In bed by Midnight- awake again at 7am for work.  Ugh.  I haven't had a chance to clean up the digital photos I shot... should have some shortly.<P>Thanks to everyone for finding me!  I'm not good with names either... and everyone else above has mentioned pretty much everyone else I recall (oh yeah... talked to Old Lars while it rained, and GM_parts_guy for awhile).  Monkeyman... Thanks for the taillight, I'll see what I can do with it- BTW: I loved your shirt- I've got a purple & yellow one very similiar, but my wife hates it!<P>Thanks to anyone/everyone who may have voted for me... I'm always surprised when I actually get an award- especailly in Mod/Custom/Rebody class!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000016||MinnGreenGT||09-10-2001||11:26 AM||||Now to some pics...<P>I'll start off with my traveling to Fierorama... we left Friday night and drove to Winona, MN.  I awoke saturday morning to find a nice nail (furniture tack actually) firmly embedded in my tire.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tirenail1.jpg">   <BR>Nail firmly embedded!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tirenail2.jpg">   <BR>Bit of a tight working space, but not bad.<BR>Notice my brother's GT in the background- too bad he didn't come... his car is pretty rough though.<P>So, after running out to get a tire patch kit and delaying or departure by an hour, we were back on the road!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carissa1.jpg">   <BR>My wife keeping warm.  <BR>No heater core= REALLY cold air all the time!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/robdriving1.jpg">   <BR>Me driving... all the way... a little bored.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/crusingspeed.jpg">   <BR>Cruising along above 80mph.  Thank God for the 4spd... just wish my TCC would lock up. I'd drop about 500rpm off the tach reading.<P>Next day at the show...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/greendisplay1.jpg">   <BR>My car... as usual- tough to photograph the green.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/greendisplay2.jpg">   <BR>Another of my car... I didn't get around much with the camera, cause it started to rain about then...<P>More coming...<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||MinnGreenGT||09-10-2001||11:52 AM||||...continued<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/greenrain1.jpg">    <BR>My (wet) GreenGT<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FR_raining01.jpg">    <BR>It started to dump the rain... people filled McDonald's and headed for cover.  Those with umbrellas and ponchos still wandered the field.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/warberwinner.jpg">    <BR>This car won the "Warber" award in memory of Mr.Warber-  conviently parked right next to mine!  WOW! what a car.<P>After the awards show, the rain let up for the most part (figures...)<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FR_field02.jpg">    <BR>People heading out...<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FR_field01.jpg">    <BR>...and cleaning up.<P><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wet_moocow1.jpg">    <BR>I happened to snap a quick shot of MooCow's Yellow GT when I was getting ready to pull out of the lot.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sunset1.jpg">    <BR>And finally on our way home we were met with on again- off again rain showers... and a colorful cloudy sunset.<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||LAMBO||09-10-2001||12:23 PM||||Haze, Congrats on winning some awards with the Indy. I knew it could be a winner, just needed someone like you to get it there. Good to see the car is being well taken care of. Later, Todd||||reg||14
Z||000019||Haze_ette||09-10-2001||12:47 PM||||Hi Everyone!!<BR>I know you all are dying to see Haze (and everyone else that they interviewed) on Motorsports Unlimited. So, here is the link to their website. (There is a page that lists the channels so that you can find where the show is on in your area!!) <A HREF="http://www.msutv.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.msutv.com</A> <BR>I guess the show will be on in about 5 weeks or so.<P>It was great seeing everyone on Sunday.<P>Lady Pegasus - "keep singing in the rain!" (let me know about Friday!)<P>Talk to everyone soon!<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000020||Bill Osmer||09-10-2001||02:09 PM||||Congrats to everyone!! It was one heck of a day - after figuring it was going to rain, me and my buddy from Granger decided we'd chance it anyway to be with other Fiero crazies - and we found them!! Besides my "Service Engine" light coming on, the rest of the trip was worth it. (Wish I could figure out how to get more votes!!)<P>Glad to see and meet all of you:<BR>- Pats86GT<P>- the NIFE regulars<P>- Oreif<BR>- Monkeyman(It was great meeting you & your wife)<BR>- Tina- Nice meeting you. Glad you could make the distance!<BR>- Haze  <BR>- Chris Moore (he ALWAYS wins, no matter what he brings!)<BR>- Lothar - you da man!!<BR>- Rodney - hope you got dry!!<BR>- Nolan (the chrome god) - thanks<BR>- Doug Kinney (Fierowarehouse)<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Bill Osmer (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000021||87 Pegasus||09-10-2001||07:55 PM||||After much thinking about it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> i have decided to forgive you Oreif...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I would like to congradulate everyone one who went home with a Trophie (class winner sheet) It was nice getting a chance to put faces with cars...  Thank you MinnGreenGT for the Checker Board background.  <BR>Haze-ette I will make sure Lady Pegasus will give you a call to set things up...  Oh yeah by the way The Classic Pegasus on the Hood of my car will no longer be Drag strip pin striping...  I have decided to get it air brushed on.  if anyone has any ideas of different Pegasus's to use please few feel to post them and i will take a look at them... if not i will draw my own...  it will either be 2-D or a 3-D one.  i will keep everyone updated...     <P><BR>------------------<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!<p>[This message has been edited by 87 Pegasus (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000022||Leadfoot||09-10-2001||09:18 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR>[BPeople heading out...<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FR_field01.jpg">      <BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey thats me on the very left, to my right is Gargoyle.  Behind him is Rich and to the right of Rich is the man who needs no introduction...Oreif.  Man was my whole backside soaked!<P><p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||Dave Gunsul||09-10-2001||09:48 PM||||I think we should rename the event and call it fiRAINorama next year.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Congrats to all the winners (especially 87 Peg. since he was forgotten above  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>It was very nice to meet the people from the forum that came to the show. The MI group was<BR>especially fun and friendly!<P>I'd also like to say that the pizza party on<BR>saturday was fun too. Archie picked up the tab for us all. Thanks Archie!!<BR>I would also like to thank Moo Cow again for letting me drive his 3.4 powered 87 GT with the 4:10 4-speed. This was quite a treat!<BR>This is a hot car believe me!!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000024||MooCow||09-10-2001||09:55 PM||||It was so much fun I want another one.  My car had to get parked next to a Buick the whole time.  I was pretty mad about that, but new I didnt stand a chance at winning so it was all good. Nice meeting everyone.  Also Monkey man got a new masscott from one of my friends. He bought a monkey off of him for $5.  Congrats on everyone that won.<BR>Thanks for posting my car MinnGreenGT<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
